{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTabBar"},"kind":"symbol","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/oudscomponents\/oudstabbar"]}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/7SwiftUI4ViewP"],"kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"@","kind":"attribute"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:ScM","text":"MainActor","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSTabBar","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Content","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7SwiftUI4ViewP","text":"View","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/Navigations"]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Appearances","anchor":"Appearances"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"iOS 26 brings Liquid Glass, the new Apple look and feel which will prevent developers to define specific styles for some critical components like bars."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Because today the OUDS tab bar relies on native component and is not designed from scratch, some elements will look different between iOS 26 and older versions:"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"background color of tab bar can be changed for iOS lower than 26","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"background color of tab bar does not change since iOS 26","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"normal \/ unselected tab item color can be changed for both image and text only for iOS lower than 26","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"with iOS 26 no token of color are applied on unselected \/ normal tab item because only the image will be changed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and not the text making theme not readable in dark color scheme","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In addition the badges colors will be the same and cannot be changed (except with token definition). These particular badges do not rely on "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSBadgeStandard","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"or "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSBadgeCount","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":", the native API is used instead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because Liquid Glass is available since iOS 26, the tab bar will be liquified \/ glassified since this OS version, not before."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"However if an app is built with Xcode 26 and the flag "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"UIDesignRequiresCompatibility"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" set to "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"YES"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":", then Liquid Glass won’t be applied but the alternative layout."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Nevertheless with Xcode 27 and for iOS 27, Liquid Glass will be always applied, whatever the value of the flag is."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you use SF Symbols for images, if they exist their "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"fill"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" variant will be automatically used in the tab bar (native behaviour)."}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Platform considerations","anchor":"Platform-considerations"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This component is tailored for iOS","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On iPadOS the tabs do not apply the fonts since iPadOS 18","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Because macOS does not support UIKit and because UIKIt is used to define the style of the tab bar, there is no styling of the tab bar for macOS","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"visionOS with its specific UI does not apply colors on tab bars and things are glasssified","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The component is not available for watchOS","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The component is not available for tvOS","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Guidelines","anchor":"Guidelines"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDS guidelines recommends to:","type":"text"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"limit when possible the number of items to 5"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"use both images and texts in tab bar items"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"use badges only when needed to avoid to have heavy tab bar"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"be sure the selected information is not only defined by the color of the tab; you may need to change the shape or the fill of the image"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"if a badge must be displayed, prefer short texts. If the text is a decimal value greater than 99, prefer display “+99”"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"if decorative images are used for tab bar item, apply "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"template"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rendering mode on it to apply color on tabs"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","text":"Accessibility considerations","level":2,"anchor":"Accessibility-considerations"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If your tabs embedded in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSTabBar"},{"type":"text","text":" do not contain texts but only images, add an accessibility label introducing the journey for this tab"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If your tabs embedded in the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSTabBar"},{"text":" display a badge (empty or with text), vocalize it in your tab to let users know what it is (unread messages, new things, etc)","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"by using accessibiltiy value","type":"text"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["    OUDSTabBar {","        SomeView()","            .tabItem {","                Label {","                    Text(\"Emails\") \/\/ The text is vocalized first","                        .accessibilityValue(\"5 unread emails\") \/\/ A value vocalized after the text","            } icon: {","                Image(systemName: \"mail\").accessibilityHidden(true)","            }","        }","        .badge(5) \/\/ The value you give to the badge","    }",""]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Selection of tabs","anchor":"Selection-of-tabs"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For iOS lower than 26, a selected tab indicator is displayed in the "},{"code":"OUDSTabBar","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" ; the "},{"code":"count","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" parameter must be defined (to the number of tabs in the component),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and if the "},{"code":"selectedTab","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" binding value is equal to a given tag associated to a tab item."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Otherwise the indicator won’t appear; these parameters are mandatory to compute the location of the indicator."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"This rule is only applied if selected tab indicator must be displayed."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"When the user taps a tab, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"selectedTab"},{"type":"text","text":" binding is updated automatically, keeping the parent view in sync."}]},{"anchor":"Technical-considerations","type":"heading","text":"Technical considerations","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"In order to improve the Developer eXperience the current "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSTabBar"},{"type":"text","text":" implementation lets users define their own tab items."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"OUDS applies only appearances and styles on elements to prevent users to define raw data to assign to the component before being rendered like a "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"picker"}]},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Thus users will need to add their own accessiiblity label if badges are used or also apply "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"template"}]},{"type":"text","text":" rendering mode on images if needed."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"Thus it will be also possible to use Liquid Glass new API with animations and items stacking.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You must use in your tab bar items images with "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"a size of 26 x 26","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":", otherwise rendering could be unaligned with Figma specifications"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Because the component cannot compute the ideal width of the selected tab indicator (for iOS before 26 and iPadOS before 18), ideal width based on the tab bar item content,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this indicator is not displayed for iOS lower than 26 in landscape mode and iPadOS."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If your app uses several universes with nested views, containing their own navigation and tab bars, prefer "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"hideTabBar()"},{"type":"text","text":" from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"View"},{"type":"text","text":" to hide the tab bar"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TabView"},{"type":"text","text":" and overlay items) with Liquid Glass is disabled or not available, or also "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tabBar(isHidden:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Code samples","anchor":"Code-samples"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["    \/\/ Use the OUDS tab bar to wrap tab bar items and associated views","    \/\/ Item tagged 0 will be selected first, 3 tabs are embedded.","    \/\/ Image with size of 26 x 26","    @State private var selectedTab = 0","","    OUDSTabBar(selectedTab: $selectedTab, count: 3) {","","        \/\/ Add the views with the SwiftUI tab item and labels","        \/\/ No need to define colors, everything is done inside OUDSTabBar","        SomeView()","            .tabItem {","                Label(\"Label 1\", image: \"image_1\")","            }","            .tag(0) \/\/ Must match the selectedTab binding value","        OtherView()","            .tabItem {","                Label {","                    Text(\"Label 2\")","                } icon: {","                    Image(decorative: \"image_2\")","                        .renderingMode(.template) \/\/ Mandatory to apply color on selected item","                }","             }","            .tag(1) \/\/ Must be used for the selectedTab binding","        LastView()","            .tabItem {","                Label(\"Label 3\", image: \"image_3\")","            }","            .tag(2) \/\/ Must be used for the selectedTab binding","    }"]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Alternative components","anchor":"Alternative-components"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"If you want to use SwiftUI ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tab","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" View with or without rules, use instead ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSTabView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"If you target apps with Liquid Glass enabled and need ","type":"text"},{"code":"Tab","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" or rules, use instead ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSLiquidGlassTabView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Design documentation","anchor":"Design-documentation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/r.orange.fr\/r\/S-ouds-doc-ios-tab-bar","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]},{"level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Themes rendering","anchor":"Themes-rendering"},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Liquid Glass","anchor":"Liquid-Glass"},{"level":4,"anchor":"Orange","type":"heading","text":"Orange"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_tabBar_LiquidGlass_Orange_light"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"image","identifier":"component_tabBar_LiquidGlass_Orange_dark"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":4,"anchor":"Orange-Compact","type":"heading","text":"Orange Compact"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"component_tabBar_LiquidGlass_OrangeCompact_light"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"image","identifier":"component_tabBar_LiquidGlass_OrangeCompact_dark"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"Sosh","anchor":"Sosh"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_tabBar_LiquidGlass_Sosh_light","type":"image"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"component_tabBar_LiquidGlass_Sosh_dark","type":"image"}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"Wireframe","anchor":"Wireframe"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_tabBar_LiquidGlass_Wireframe_light","type":"image"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"component_tabBar_LiquidGlass_Wireframe_dark","type":"image"}]},{"level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Without Liquid Glass","anchor":"Without-Liquid-Glass"},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"Orange","anchor":"Orange"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_tabBar_Orange_light","type":"image"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"component_tabBar_Orange_dark","type":"image"}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"Orange Compact","anchor":"Orange-Compact"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_tabBar_OrangeCompact_light","type":"image"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"component_tabBar_OrangeCompact_dark","type":"image"}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"Sosh","anchor":"Sosh"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_tabBar_Sosh_light","type":"image"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"component_tabBar_Sosh_dark","type":"image"}]},{"level":4,"type":"heading","text":"Wireframe","anchor":"Wireframe"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"component_tabBar_Wireframe_light","type":"image"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"component_tabBar_Wireframe_dark","type":"image"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1.0.0 (Figma component design version)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Version"},{"type":"aside","style":"note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"1.0.0","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Since"}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Components"}],"platforms":[{"name":"iOS","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"15.0","deprecated":false},{"name":"macOS","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"13.0","deprecated":false},{"name":"visionOS","unavailable":false,"beta":false,"introducedAt":"1.0","deprecated":false}],"symbolKind":"struct","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"OUDSTabBar","kind":"identifier"}],"title":"OUDSTabBar","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"OUDSTabBar","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:14OUDSComponents10OUDSTabBarV"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Tab bar is a system navigation component with a position which can vary depending to the OS."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The tab bar can be found at the bottom of the screen for iOS. It can vary for iPadOS."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It allows users to switch between the sections of an app."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Each tab can be represented by a label, optionally paired with an icon, and maintains persistent visibility across top-level destinations."}],"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents"]]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTabBar\/init(content:)","doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTabBar\/init(selectedTab:count:content:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","generated":true},{"title":"Instance Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/OUDSComponents\/documentation\/OUDSComponents\/OUDSTabBar\/body"],"anchor":"Instance-Properties","generated":true},{"title":"Default Implementations","identifiers":["doc:\/\/O